mainmenu "hello_world (ADC->BLE pipeline test)"

menu "ADC->BLE pipeline parameters (HW-only, do not treat as validated)"

config SM_SAMPLE_RATE_HR_HZ
	int "PULSE_WINDOW sample rate for heart-rate windows (Hz)"
	default 200
	help
	  Unused by this project (PULSE_WINDOW is never entered here — see
	  main.c), kept only because sampling_source.c/sampling_source_nrfx.c
	  were ported unmodified from nrf5340_firmware and still reference
	  it for sm_window_profiles[]/buffer sizing.

config SM_SAMPLE_RATE_BP_HZ
	int "PULSE_WINDOW sample rate for blood-pressure/PTT windows (Hz)"
	default 1000
	help
	  Unused by this project, same reason as SM_SAMPLE_RATE_HR_HZ above.

config SM_SAMPLE_RATE_ACTIVITY_HZ
	int "ACTIVE_CAPTURE sample rate (Hz)"
	default 500
	help
	  The rate actually used: this project's state machine is locked
	  into ACTIVE_CAPTURE for the whole session (see main.c).
	  ble_sender.c streams live (see its own header comment) rather than
	  buffering a session in RAM, so this needs to stay within BLE's
	  actual sustained throughput or ble_sender.c's TX queue will start
	  dropping windows — real-hardware testing put sustained throughput
	  at roughly 14-15 fragments/s post-connection; at
	  BLE_SM_SAMPLES_PER_PKT=50 (see ble_sender.c) this rate needs 2
	  fragments per 100-sample window, so 500 Hz's 5 windows/s (10
	  frag/s) has real margin where 1000 Hz's 10 windows/s (20 frag/s)
	  did not. HW-only: real value TBD once front-end requirements are
	  confirmed — do not treat as final.

config SM_PULSE_WINDOW_MS
	int "PULSE_WINDOW duration (ms)"
	default 3000
	help
	  Unused by this project (PULSE_WINDOW is never entered here), kept
	  because sampling_source_nrfx.c still sizes its pulse_buf[] from it.

config SM_SILENCE_TIMEOUT_MS
	int "ACTIVE_CAPTURE silence timeout (ms)"
	default 86400000
	help
	  How long without a fresh EV_ACTIVITY before ACTIVE_CAPTURE exits
	  back to DEEP_IDLE. Deliberately set to 24 hours (vs.
	  nrf5340_firmware's 2000 ms default) so this simplified pipeline's
	  single boot-time EV_ACTIVITY kick (see main.c) keeps it sampling
	  for the whole session — nothing here ever posts a follow-up
	  EV_ACTIVITY the way sm_event_injection.c does in the source
	  project. sm_core.c's actual exit logic is untouched; this just
	  keeps it from ever firing in practice.

config SM_ACTIVITY_CHUNK_SAMPLES
	int "ACTIVE_CAPTURE ping-pong chunk size (samples per channel)"
	default 100
	help
	  How many samples (per channel) fill one ping-pong buffer before
	  EV_BUF_READY fires. Trade-off between handoff latency and
	  per-buffer overhead — HW-only, real value TBD.

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
